<spell-notebook "message theming">
	<header level="1">
		Message
		<header>A message displays information that explains nearby content.</>
	</>
	<message-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-message-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every
			message), or on the box through `::part(message)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each
			through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. A slotted header reads `--ui-message-header-font-size`
			from the message. Style the other pieces with `::part()`: `icon`, `content`, `header` and `close`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			:root {
			  --ui-message-radius: 0;
			}
			ui-message.notice {
			  --ui-message-padding: 1.5em 2em;
			}
			ui-message::part(close) {
			  opacity: 1;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`state` and `color` are colour remaps: they re-point `--ui-color` and its tints, so a theme recolours every
				positive or red message by setting `--ui-positive` / `--ui-red`. Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the
				sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-message" playground>
				<ui-message>
					<ui-header>Changes in Service</>
					<ui-text paragraph>We just updated our privacy policy here to better service our customers. We recommend reviewing the changes.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
